Upstream-Name: SVXConnect-Qt
Upstream-Contact: Joeri Van Dooren <ure@on6ure.be>
Source: https://github.com/Guru-RF/SVXConnect-Debian
Comment:
 SVXConnect-Qt links the Qt toolkit dynamically under the GNU Lesser General
 Public License version 3. Qt is a dependency satisfied by the distribution's
 own packages and is not conveyed by this package, which is LGPL-3.0 section
 4d1; the full texts are at /usr/share/common-licenses/LGPL-3 and
 /usr/share/common-licenses/GPL-3, and both are needed because the LGPL is
 written as additional permissions on top of the GPL. Only LGPL-licensed Qt
 modules are used — Qt Charts, Qt Graphs, Qt Data Visualization, Qt WebEngine
 and several others are GPL-3.0-only in the open-source edition, and linking
 one would make this binary GPLv3 while this file said Expat. That is enforced
 at configure time by cmake/LicenceGuard.cmake and again against the linked
 binary by tools/licence_guard.sh, which debian/rules runs during the build.
 .
 The full third-party notice, including the LGPL relink statement required by
 section 4, is installed as
 /usr/share/doc/svxconnect-qt/THIRD-PARTY-NOTICES.
 .
 The reflector protocol, TLS, AES-GCM and Opus layers originate in the
 copyright holder's own prior C work. No code from the upstream SvxLink project
 (GPL-2.0) is used.

